{
  "tema": 5588,
  "slug": "he-comido-perfecto-er-ir",
  "titulo": "Regular -er and -ir verbs in the present perfect",
  "subtitulo": "¿Has comido? Hemos vivido aquí diez años.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "The present perfect is haber in the present (he, has, ha, hemos, han) + the participle. For -er and -ir verbs, the participle ends in -ido: comer → he comido, vivir → he vivido.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Same structure as with -ar verbs: **haber** in the present + the **past participle**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For **-er** and **-ir** verbs, drop the ending and add **-ido**: **comer → comido**, **vivir → vivido**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "he / has / ha / hemos / han",
            "+ stem +",
            "-ido"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "comer",
            "vivir"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**he** comido",
              "**he** vivido"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**has** comido",
              "**has** vivido"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "**ha** comido",
              "**ha** vivido"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "**hemos** comido",
              "**hemos** vivido"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "**han** comido",
              "**han** vivido"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Stem changes of the present **don't** go into the participle: **dormir → dormido**, **pedir → pedido**, **poder → podido**. Even **ser → sido** and **ir → ido** are regular."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When the stem ends in **a**, **e** or **o**, write an accent: **leer → leído**, **creer → creído**, **traer → traído**, **oír → oído**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The participle never changes, and nothing goes between **haber** and it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==He comido== demasiado.",
              "en": "I've eaten too much."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Has vivido== siempre en Tijuana?",
              "en": "Have you always lived in Tijuana?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hijo ==ha aprendido== a nadar este verano.",
              "en": "My son has learned to swim this summer."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Hemos dormido== muy poco esta semana.",
              "en": "We've slept very little this week."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ustedes ya ==han pedido==?",
              "en": "Have you guys ordered yet?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Nunca ==he leído== los libros de The Expanse.",
              "en": "I've never read The Expanse books."
            },
            {
              "es": "Las lechugas ==han crecido== mucho con la lluvia.",
              "en": "The lettuces have grown a lot with the rain."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Has salido== a correr hoy?",
              "en": "Have you gone out running today?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
